Z||000006||Blade||08-22-2000||01:57 AM||||AL...Im in orange county.<BR>nother question for whoever. Owner im getting this car from says he has taken it up to 135 is this possible with a stock engine?<P>Blade||||reg||1
Z||000007||86SE||08-22-2000||02:04 AM||||With a stock engine I hightly doubt it.  You will need at least 200-230 Hp to even get close.<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfiero||08-22-2000||02:09 AM||||It's very doubtful that he got it anywhere north of 120 MPH.  Stock Fieros "lift" at high speeds, which creates one he!! of a drag.  My stock 16K mile GT barely hits 118 MPH (much less if it's windy)......stock Fieros ride very high on their suspensions, which doesn't help things out.  <P>I did own a lowred 5-sp. '88 Formula with a mildly built 2.8 and it felt very strong around 120.....I would say it topped out around 125.<P>The speedo stops at 120, so anything higher than that would be speculation, unless verified by a radar gun.<P>Just an opinion....BTW, the '86 & '87 SE could be ordered with either the 4-cyl. or V-6.  They looked identical, but they all didn't have V-6's.<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||fldevel||08-22-2000||01:18 PM||||anyting above 100 mph in a fiero would be suiside ..<BR>i was once clocked by a cop doing 128 mph ..he asked me if i knew how fast i was going and i sed " no sir my speedo only goes up to 85" ...i got off with a warning  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||HugGRRRFiero||08-22-2000||01:44 PM||||Welcome to the forum Blade!  135 MPH is pretty optimistic but possible under a closed course and with a professional driver.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  I've got an 85 speedo too, so I couldn't tell you what mine does.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Brent<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||6
Z||000011||wahoo4u||08-22-2000||04:13 PM||||welcome.  good to see yet another 86 SE still on the road.  I also have a 86 SE v6 i don't believe that it will hit 135.  So far, the best I could get out of mine was between 125 and 130.  Following a friend with a speedo that went to 140 so it should be fairly accurate.  With that right conditions, i think it should hit 130.  Just hang on tight, it is one awesome ride.  Congrats.||||reg||6
